# StageVerify lean agent process (D-94)

SSOT for review lanes, merge/deploy, and always-loaded rules. **Supersedes D-60 and D-65.** Amends D-92 / D-93 (Composer still codes; extra model passes run only when this file says so). Older `.cursor/rules/*` files are on-demand — if they conflict with this file, **this file wins**.

## One job

One small job per agent. PR body: what changed, why, how to test, rollback. No reviewer swarms.

## Risk tiers (classify by path before you edit)

**HIGH** — `firestore.rules`; auth / PIN / roles (client or CF); Cloud Functions that **write** core-loop data (invoice approve, spot assign / reassign, vendor drop-off, tech pickup, spot release); billing; CI / gate config (`.github/workflows/`, `firebase.json`, `scripts/gate-check.mjs`, `scripts/install-git-hooks.mjs`, root `package.json` scripts / deploy wiring). Ambiguous → HIGH.

**MEDIUM** — other backend or multi-file changes that are not HIGH.

**LOW** — UI, copy, docs, `PROJECT_STATUS/`, on-demand rules.

## Reviews

- Composer 2.5 Fast does all routine coding (UI and non-UI).
- **HIGH:** one Grok top-model review of the **final** diff (`cursor-grok-4.6-high`; `cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh` also allowed). Record `security-gate-id:` (lowercase UUID or `bc-<uuid>`) **and** `model: <slug used>`. Reject `NOT RUN`, empty, and junk. This **replaces** `sonnet-instruct`, `high-risk-adversarial`, and `sonnet-verify`.
- **MEDIUM:** one cheap Grok review of the final diff. No `security-gate-id`.
- **LOW:** no AI review.
- **Sonnet escalation (optional — never default):** `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` only for `firestore.rules`, auth/PIN/roles, or billing/money; **or** when the Grok HIGH review returns FAIL / a HIGH finding; **or** when Dan asks. No other default Sonnet use.
- **Dropped:** `solution-verifier`, `build-checker`, `ship-verifier`. Do not run them.
- **UI screenshots:** only for **big** visual changes (theme, contrast, complex layout, redesign). Not for copy, labels, or small CSS.

HIGH review how-to (on-demand): `.cursor/rules/security-review-gate.mdc`. Cloud agents may record `security-gate-id: bc-<uuid>` from a real security-review run — do not invent ids.

## Tests are the safety net

CI on every PR must pass: `npm ci`, app build, functions build, `tsc`, and the Firestore emulator suites in `.github/workflows/pr-ci.yml`. Do not merge on red CI.

## Non-negotiables

1. A **real recorded** HIGH review (`security-gate-id:` + `model:`).
2. Tests and the build pass before merge.
3. **Dan approves every merge and every deploy.** No auto-merge. No auto-deploy. Draft PRs are the default from cloud.
4. A **rollback point** (commit hash / prior CF revision) before every deploy, and a **smoke test** after.
5. **No gate bypass.** Do not use `GATE_SKIP`, `--no-verify`, or forged ids to skip HIGH review.
6. One small job per agent; notes in the PR body.

## Merge and deploy

Branch + PR. Dan merges. Dan authorizes deploy (gh-pages, Cloud Functions, Firestore rules) separately. After deploy: smoke the path you changed; keep the rollback hash ready.

## Minew / NDA

Never commit or paste Minew API docs, credentials, or platform internals. HTTP calls server-side only (`functions/src/`). Public UI uses StageVerify QR URLs (`#/r?`, `#/p?`) only.
